audio.cpp fork delta: the ggml_ssm_scan_set_fusion API and one more im2col
lowering value, ported 2026-09-23. Source commit: audio.cpp #600 (82b4dc3a,
"Add opt-in CUDA SSM gate fusion and tiled F32 im2col") - header and ggml.c
hunks only.

  - enum ggml_ssm_scan_fusion {NONE, GATE} and ggml_ssm_scan_set_fusion().
  - GGML_IM2COL_2D_LOWERING_CUDA_F32_K3_TILED.

DELIBERATE DIVERGENCE from audio.cpp: the fusion flag lives in op_params slot 1,
not slot 0. audio.cpp's ggml predates ggml-org's "recurrent state rollback"
(llama/26623), which made slot 0 of SSM_SCAN the state count K (asserted >= 1
by the CPU and CUDA kernels). Writing FUSION_NONE (0) to slot 0 would set K=0.
Whoever ports the CUDA fused kernel must read the flag from slot 1.

NOT PORTED YET: the CUDA side of 82b4dc3a (ssm-scan.cu[h] fused gate,
ggml-cuda.cu can_fuse / try_fuse, im2col.cu tiled F32). Nothing in the engine
calls ggml_ssm_scan_set_fusion today, so the flag is inert.

